{
  "program": "CBTRN03C",
  "caseId": "case19",
  "description": "The two right-truncating moves of 1120-WRITE-DETAIL. TRAN-TYPE-DESC is PIC X(50) in app/cpy/CVTRA03Y.cpy moving into TRAN-REPORT-TYPE-DESC PIC X(15) at :366, and TRAN-CAT-TYPE-DESC is PIC X(50) in app/cpy/CVTRA04Y.cpy moving into TRAN-REPORT-CAT-DESC PIC X(29) at :368. An alphanumeric MOVE fills the receiver from its leftmost position and discards what does not fit on the RIGHT, so both descriptions keep their leading characters and lose their tails. Neither shipped fixture can prove it - no trantype description exceeds fifteen characters and no trancatg description exceeds twenty-nine - so both lookup datasets are seeded here with genuine 60-byte records built to their copybooks' shape and carrying descriptions that occupy all fifty bytes.",
